      "title": "Why Segments ?",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "In certain situations, placing an object entirely within a single tile is essential for achieving consistent results. By applying a mask to an object, it can be sampled separately from the rest of the image. The masked area will then be upscaled to match the tile size, enhancing its detail.\n\nThis technique can also be used to repair or modify elements by applying different settings, prompts, or denoise values using the function.\n\nAfter the entire image is processed, the segmented areas will be handled. ImpactPack is compatible with TBG ETUR segmentation entries, making it possible to automate the selection process."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
