      "title": "Only Upscale",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Set the Lab Node to Only Upscale to turn this into a fully functional Tiled Upscaler without prepairing things for the refiner.\n\nWe fine-tuned SeedVR2, Waifu, FlashVR, and others into a new multi-step Upscaler with adaptive sigmas.\nGive them a try — they’re not the fastest option, but for consistent, high-quality upscaling, this is a solid solution.\n\nFor more details on what’s changed, please read the text field shown when creating the node and have a look into the Tooltips."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 78,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1712.5946267434558,
        1596.3782444593712
      ],
      "size": [
        538.7564999999995,
        183.923
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 2,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Denoise Mask",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "We have three ways to load VLMs:\n\n1. **Standard** – Fully automatic setup. Supports all models except GGUF.\n\n2. **GGUF** – Often requires a manual llama.cpp server installation, which can be complicated for some configurations. We provide prebuilt wheels, and installation is only required if you select the GGUF option.\n\n3. **Fastest and Best Option: OpenAI-Compatible (Labs Server)** – Connect the Labs_upscaler node and enter the URL, port, and model name of your local or API-based Ollama or llama.cpp server with the Qwen GGUF model loaded.\n\n4. Florence has now been fixed to run on Transformer versions 5 and above.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
