      "title": "Reference Images (Flux2 / QwenEdit/Kontext )",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "How to use the new reference-image ControlNet-style mode\n\nThis new mode lives in the `TBG ControlNet Pipe` node and works like a familiar ControlNet slider setup, but under the hood it is still a latent correction path, not a real ControlNet model.\n\n1. Add a `TBG ControlNet Pipe` node to your workflow.\n\n2. Set `reference_mode` to `Reference ControlNet` - it auto feeds the tile as ref.\n\n3. Set the three new sliders:\n\n   - `Strength` = how strongly the reference pulls the denoised latent\n\n   - `Start %` = when the influence starts\n\n   - `End %` = when the influence stops\n\n4. Connect the `Controlnet_Pipe` output into your `TBG ETUR Refiner PRO` node’s `Controlnet_Pipe` input.\n\nBy setting the Preprocessor dropdown to None, the reference image will use the full-color tile. Selecting Depth uses a depth map as the reference image, while Canny uses a canny edge map. You can also combine and chain them together. If you connect an image to the slot in the ControlNet pipe, that image will be used as the reference image for all tiles.\n\nImportant note:\nWhen strength is set to 1 (start = 0, end = 1), the node injects the reference image in the standard behavior. For all other values, the reference image is injected on a per-step basis, which behaves differently. If you want to use both modes simultaneously, you need to use two ControlNet Pipe nodes—one for each mode.\n have both use 2 controlnet pipe nodes 1 for each."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1465.249655005081,
        3440.644173574323
      ],
      "size": [
        450,
        220
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "ControlNets",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "You can add as many ControlNets as you like.\ncurrently, the only available preprocessors are Depth, Canny, Canny Edge, and None. We’ve excluded Pose because the subject will be divided into tiles, making pose estimation ineffective in the cnet pipe you can add pose conventionaly to the croped conditioning in the refiner.\n\nA global ControlNet strength modifier is available to help fine-tune all ControlNets at once.\n\nThe ControlNet preprocessor works directly on each tile, allowing it to operate at the tile's full resolution. This differs from other refiners like Ultimate Upscale, where the ControlNet input is cropped, and a tile only uses a small portion of the full ControlNet resolution. With our setup, each tile benefits from full-resolution preprocessing."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
